<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 31 0 R
/E (Akhanda-bhajan must be as continuous as breathing itself if it is to deserve its name. You must probe into the real significance of the sankeerthan that you are engaged in. Keerthan is "singing aloud the Glory of God." Sankeerthan is the process of singing that originates in the heart, not from the lips or tongue. It is the expression of the joyous thrill that wells up from the heart when the Glory of God is remembered. It is the spontaneous manifestation of inner ecstasy, No attention is paid to the blame or praise that others may give. It does not seek the admiration or the appreciation of the listeners. It is sung for one's own joy, one's own satisfaction, one's own delight. Keerthan of this supreme type, alone, deserves the name sankeerthan )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [10]
>>
